-- title:
--   Local unit χ-eigensection of [n]_*𝒪_A
-- statement:
--   Fix an algebraically closed field $K$, a scheme $A$ and a morphism $f : A \to \operatorname{Spec} K$, together with a relative group law $L$ for $f$ (a functorial group structure, with naturality for the multiplication, on the sets $\{\varphi : T \to A \mid \varphi \circ f = t\}$ of $T$-points of $A$ over $\operatorname{Spec} K$), assumed commutative, and the hypothesis that $f$ is smooth, proper, has connected fibres and admits a relative group law; further let $g$ be a natural number with $f$ smooth of relative dimension $g$. Let $n$ be a natural number whose image in $K$ is nonzero, and suppose that for every $n$-torsion $K$-point $x$ of $L$ the composite of the translation $L.translate\ x$ with the multiplication-by-$n$ endomorphism $[n] =$ `L.schemeNsmul n` of $A$ equals $[n]$. Let $\chi$ be a $K$-valued function on the $K$-points which is $1$ off the $n$-torsion, sends the identity to $1$, and is multiplicative on the $n$-torsion. Then for every point $y$ of $A$ there is an affine open $V \subseteq A$ containing $y$ and an element $s$ of $(L.eigenSubdatum\ n\ hG\ \chi)$ over $V$, i.e. a section of $\Gamma(A, [n]^{-1}V)$ lying in the submodule cut out by the $\chi$-eigensection condition for the deck action of the $n$-torsion, such that $s$ is a unit of the ring $\Gamma(A, [n]^{-1}V)$.
--
--   This is the local step towards invertibility of the $\chi$-eigen-part $\mathcal{E}_\chi$ of $[n]_*\mathcal{O}_A$ for an abelian scheme over an algebraically closed field: near each point of $A$ the eigen-part contains a section which is a unit downstairs, so that it is locally generated by one invertible section. It feeds the statement that multiplication by such a section gives bijections between the eigen-part and the trivial eigen-part, used in the analysis of the $n$-torsion and the resulting line bundles.
